   Technol, HOME Program; Malardalen Univ, Future Energy Profile; Shanghai
   Key Lab Urban Regenerat \& Spatial Optimizat Technol; MOE Joint Lab Int
   Cooperat Eco Urban Design; Sichuan Univ; Shanghai Univ Electric Power;
   BEEUE; Int Clean Energy Talent Program; UNiLAB},
Abstract = {In this paper, Organic Rankine cycle combined power and ejector
   refrigeration system has been proposed and described in detail. The
   combine system can recycle the exhaust heat to refrigerate as compared
   to the conventional ORC system. Furthermore, the ejector refrigeration
   system has simple structure with low operating, installation and
   maintenance cost as compare to other refrigeration systems. The
   parametric model has been established to evaluate and analyze the system
   performance. REFPROP and MATLAB are used to calculate thermodynamic
   properties and simulate the results. Thermodynamic parameters including
   generator temperature, condenser temperature, evaporator temperature and
   its various effects have been investigated with respect to system
   efficiency. The simulation results showed that system efficiency and
   entrainment ratio can be enhanced by increasing the generator
   temperature and evaporator temperature and decreasing the condenser
   temperature. This combine system has good development potential by
   optimizing thermodynamic parameters to improve efficiency. Copyright
   2018 Elsevier Ltd. All rights reserved.},
