Organization = {Inst Elect \& Elect Engineers; Tokyo Univ Pharm \& Life Sci; Chia Nan
   Univ Pharm \& Sci; Int Inst Knowledge Innovat \& Invent},
Abstract = {Accurate evaluation of the values of current buildings serves as the
   important prerequisite of achieving sustainable development of the
   buildings in historical site and is also an important link of
   sustainable development of the historical site. By taking the Dutian
   Temple Historical Site in Huai'an, Jiangsu province, China, as an
   example, this study established two-level evaluation system of
   comprehensive value of the building based on analytical hierarchy
   process (AHP), formulated the scoring criteria and calculated the
   weights. Next, using ArcGIS, the current building data could be
   informationized and spatialized. According to the evaluation results,
   the buildings in the historical site can be classified into five types,
   and moreover, the corresponding five different sustainable development
   modes were proposed.},
