   URBANA CHAMPAIGN; RESOURCE TECHNOL INST},
Abstract = {This paper describes the use of mathematical procedures for simulating
   surface phenomena related to natural environmental features. Surface
   estimation methods fall into three major classes: deterministic methods,
   stochastic methods and a third class based on theories of chaos and
   fractals. This third class of methods is relatively new and therefore
   not as well developed as the first two classes.  One of the major uses
   for this class of interpolators is in the graphical representation and
   modeling of natural phenomena.},
