Abstract = {It choosed coal powder, Dagu river sludge, waste plastics and additives
   as influencing factors, arranged experiment according to U(6){*}(6(4))
   uniform table. Then by standardizing partial regression coefficient,
   analysis significance and influence order of each factor. The result
   indicated that when the combination was additive species CaO, CaO+
   Ba(OH)(2) or CaO+ Fe(2)O(3)+ Na(2)CO(3), the additive level 9g/100g coal
   powder, Dagu river sludge 30g/100g coal powder, the caloric value was
   maximum and reached 7945.919 kcal/kg. The best desulphurization
   efficiency and dechlorination effect was 37.4\%, 52.5\%, respectively,
   and the factor of waste plastic was not notable. When combination was
   additive species CaO+ MgO, additive level 9g/100g coal powder, Dagu
   river sludge 30g/100g coal powder, waste plastic 4g/100g coal powder,
   the compressive strength was maximum and the value was 7.361 MPa. The
   best desulphurization efficiency and dechlorination effect was 30.9\%,
   76\%, respectively.},
