Abstract = {Mechanisms of the anaerobic uptake of glutamate and aspartate by
   enhanced biological phosphorus removal activated sludge were
   investigated. Sludge hydrolysate with hydrochloric acid was analyzed by
   reverse phase HPLC after pre column derivatization with dabsyl-chloride.
   The experimental results indicated that glutamate is accumulated as a
   polymer consisting of gamma-aminobutyric acid and an unknown amino acid.
   On the other hand, aspartate was found to be deaminated and then
