Abstract = {Implementation of ``Public Disclosure Program{''} in Indonesia
   demonstrated by the implementation of the policy of ``Program
   Performance Rating Company (PROPER){''} in environmental management,
   whose application aims to answer the need of access to information,
   transparency and public participation related to environmental
   governance. Public participation to be used as input very valuable in
   the assessment PROPER felt important. Due to there are various forms of
   complaints related to environmental issues are detected, and involving
   companies PROPER participants from various sectors that are not recorded
   in the assessment PROPER. For this study aims to be the public
   perception may be referred to as a determinant of final grades in rank
   environmental governance has made a single business unit. The approach
   taken in this study is a qualitative approach, the research respondents
   are communities around the company PROPER participants. Data collection
   techniques include in-depth interviews, observation and documentation
   studies, while data analysis techniques include: data reduction, data
   presentation, data interpretation, and conclusion. The results showed
   that (1) At this time the Society has not been actively involved in the
   implementation of PROPER assessment so that it is not in conformity with
   the goals of policy application PROPER; (2) The involvement of the
   community as one of the assessment criteria to rank the performance of
   the company in environmental management is important during the
   assessment with the aim of raising the credibility of the assessment or
   outcome PROPER.},
