Abstract = {A novel process of CO2 sequestration in mixtures of sodium humate
   (HA-Na) and waste gypsum was proposed. Experiments investigated the CO2
   absorption properties for HA-Na solution. HA-Na solution shows great
   performance in CO2 absorption, and the CO2 absorption amount reaches to
   0.96 mol for 3 hours with 100 mL HA-Na solution (0.04 g/mL), at the
   condition of 15 degrees C, gas flow rate of 40 mL/h. the CO2
   sequestration mechanism by HA-Na and desulfurization gypsum (DG) was
   analyzed. CaSO4 plays a key role in the CO2 absorption by HA-Na
   solution. A permanent method of CO2 sequestration is achieved by the
   mixtures of HA-Na and waste gypsum.},
